{"actions":[{"actionCode":"H11000","actionDate":"2025-01-08","source":"House committee actions","text":"Referred to the Subcommittee on Highways and Transit.","type":"Committee"},{"actionCode":"H11100","actionDate":"2025-01-07","source":"House floor actions","text":"Referred to the House Committee on Transportation and Infrastructure.","type":"IntroReferral"},{"actionCode":"Intro-H","actionDate":"2025-01-07","source":"Library of Congress","text":"Introduced in House","type":"IntroReferral"},{"actionCode":"1000","actionDate":"2025-01-07","source":"Library of Congress","text":"Introduced in House","type":"IntroReferral"}],"congress":119,"congressGovUrl":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/234","cosponsors":[{"bioguideId":"B001307","fullName":"Rep. Baird, James R. [R-IN-4]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-01-14","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"IN"},{"bioguideId":"S001212","fullName":"Rep. Stauber, Pete [R-MN-8]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-01-22","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"MN"},{"bioguideId":"V000138","fullName":"Rep. Vindman, Eugene Simon [D-VA-7]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2025-10-17","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"VA"},{"bioguideId":"G000583","fullName":"Rep. Gottheimer, Josh [D-NJ-5]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2026-08-24","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"NJ"}],"fetchedAt":"2026-09-20T13:54:17+00:00","id":"hr234-119","introducedDate":"2025-01-07","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-01-08","text":"Referred to the Subcommittee on Highways and Transit."},"laws":[],"number":"234","originChamber":"House","policyArea":"Transportation and Public Works","sponsors":[{"bioguideId":"M000317","district":11,"fullName":"Rep. Malliotakis, Nicole [R-NY-11]","party":"R","state":"NY"}],"summaries":[{"actionDate":"2025-01-07","actionDesc":"Introduced in House","text":"<p><b>HOV Lanes for Heroes Act</b></p> <p>This bill provides authority for a public authority to allow a disabled veteran to use a high occupancy vehicle (HOV) facility if such veteran has a license plate that clearly identifies the vehicle, a registered transponder, or other method of qualifying identification.</p> <p>The public authority may not charge a toll to the veteran for use of the HOV facility.</p>","updateDate":"2025-02-10T13:29:35Z","versionCode":"00"}],"title":"HOV Lanes for Heroes Act","type":"hr","updateDate":"2026-09-19T23:06:45Z","updateDateIncludingText":"2026-09-19T23:06:45Z"}
